WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.540
Donald Trump has had the luxury of being the
owner and boss basically since the beginning

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:06.879
of his career.

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:11.170
And one of the great things about being the
and boss is that in a sense you can't get

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:12.170
fired.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:17.920
Now I know that if you're the CEO of a publicly
traded company and there's a board of directors,

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.540
you might be the founder and you might be
the majority shareholder.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.789
Um, majority of the, the plurality owner rather
not majority shareholder, but you might still

00:00:26.789 --> 00:00:29.520
be forced to step down as CEO, for example.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.630
And there are some cases in which you can
be the founder and the boss and still get

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.630
fired.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:39.320
But in many situations outside of publicly
traded companies, you're effectively immune

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.930
from getting fired if you're the one in charge.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:44.300
I can't be fired from the David Pakman show.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.300
For example.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.450
I'm the majority shareholder.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.110
There's no board of directors.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.340
Every paid member could quit.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:52.930
Every viewer could stop watching.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.000
We could end up with effectively no show.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.820
I could just be sitting here doing videos
that nobody sees, but I can't be fired in

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.820
a sense.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.550
And that is not typical in most jobs.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.390
You're behavior on and off the job can get
you fired.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.670
And I was thinking over the weekend that Donald
Trump's behavior at any other job where he

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.560
is not the owner of the company or the person
in charge would have absolutely gotten him

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.560
fired.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:23.110
By now, Donald Trump has publicly insulted,
countless world leaders, sort of equivalent

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.700
to being our business partners.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:31.140
We can say in a sense, if anybody ranging
from a low level employee to the CEO were

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:36.790
to publicly insult their company's clients
or their customers or their partners in the

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:42.000
way that Donald Trump has insulted the leaders
of other world, uh, uh, countries, they would

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.700
have been fired by now.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:51.000
The highest law enforcement agencies in the
country did an investigation into Donald Trump

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:57.250
and they found substantial evidence of criminality
on eight of 14 possible obstruction counts

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.600
at any other job.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:05.630
Those results from a criminal investigation
would obviously get you fired and most people

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.810
would also be indicted and facing prison time
right now.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.960
But Trump's the boss or the owner or whatever
role he has as president of the United States

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.790
of America, he's apparently immune there as
well.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.390
And then there's a whole other sort of angle
on this.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:25.390
George Conway, who's an attorney and the husband
of Kellyanne Conway, who is one of Donald

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:27.390
Trump's closest advisors.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:31.010
George Conway is a big Trump opponent.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:37.040
And he pointed out something else, which is
that someone having the apparent mental health

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:44.390
issues that Donald Trump is having would also
have been let go from any other job based

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.390
on his behavior.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:50.410
Tweeting over the weekend quote, you're not
presidential at all, period.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.130
You're mentally unwell.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:58.220
You engage in bizarre, irrational self defeating
behavior, which prompts criticism of view,

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:02.150
which triggers more bizarre, irrational self
defeating behavior.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.250
You would have been fired from any other job
by now.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:12.510
Trump's behavior is the type that would get
the bosses together to say, this person needs

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:18.870
to go, let's figure out how to get them out
of here with the least amount of drama possible

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.490
and we could actually go further.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:26.490
If anybody exhibited Donald Trump's behavior
during the campaign, in the hiring process

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:30.360
for a job, they would never even get hired
in the first place.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.190
And this is what happens when instead of a
three person hiring committee, including the

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:41.100
CEO, someone from HR and a supervisor gets
to decide who to hire when it's instead left

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:46.720
up to the American people, American voters,
60 million of whom are right wing Republicans.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.510
This is exactly what you end up with.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.260
Over the weekend I was talking to a friend
who's dealing with a very similar situation

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.260
at work.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:59.460
They have a coworker who started writing outrageous,
aggressive emails including to their supervisors,

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.620
talking back to management, straight up saying
they're not going to be doing certain things

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:09.340
because as they see it, it doesn't make sense
to do it and telling the supervisors that

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:15.500
taking offense to anything that's said around
them and management is trying to figure out,

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.190
we need to get rid of this person, but we
also need to do it in a way that is not going

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:23.430
to create even more absolute and total chaos.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.800
That's the distinction with Donald Trump.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.230
Any normal person who behaved during the hiring
process, the way Donald Trump behave during

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.060
the campaign would not have been hired.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:38.490
Any person who behaved at their job the way
Donald Trump has behaved since becoming president

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.870
of the United States would have been fired.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:45.389
But the one advantage is we can just vote
Trump out.

00:04:45.389 --> 00:04:49.800
Okay, people can just go vote and Trump has
to leave period.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:57.610
In January of 2021 and my ask of you is the
following as atrocious and disastrous as Donald

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:58.780
Trump is.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:02.420
We shouldn't forget that Trump is an effect,
not a cause.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:07.420
Now, yeah, Donald Trump's presidency has caused
a lot of bad things.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.540
He's ruined relationships with allies.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.090
He's weaponized ignorance.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:13.240
He's weaponized hypocrisy.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:20.340
But Trump's presidency is the result of the
last 30 years, not a cause in and of itself.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:24.320
So remember that getting rid of Trump doesn't
actually solve the problem, although it's

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:30.210
still something that we should do, uh, but
also understand the sort of proximate causes

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:35.210
that led to Donald Trump, which is exactly
what I want to talk about next on the show,

00:05:35.210 --> 00:06:28.639
because it's so important and a lot of people
are missing the boat

00:06:28.639 --> 00:06:43.680
on this.

